    <span data-field="handbook_purpose">{{ handbook_purpose }}</span> is intended for an audience of administrators and faculty members charged with beginning a service-learning, experiential learning, or similarly focused program on a college or university campus. Our hope, as authors, is that this handbook will help you think about the complex world of community-engaged types of learning and to consider the six key focus areas that encompass a service-learning or experiential learning program: 1) Institutional support and program development; 2) Community support, participation, and partnership; 3) Faculty development, support, and involvement; 4) Student support and involvement; 5) Marketing, promotion, and events; and 6) Assessment development and implementation.
